<title>USA: Mariner Energy Inc Q1 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Mariner Energy Inc Q1 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31</p>
<p>								  Predecessor</p>
<p>									Company</p>
<p>						   Three Mos    Three Mos</p>
<p>							Ended	   Ended</p>
<p>						     Mar 31,	Mar 31,</p>
<p>							 1997	    1996</p>
<p> Total revenues				   13,683	 13,778</p>
<p> Impairment of oil and gas properties     28,514	    ---</p>
<p> Related party income				---	  2,110</p>
<p> Related party expense			     ---	  (381)</p>
<p> NET INCOME (LOSS)			    (27,632)	  2,661</p>
<p>NOTE:  &quot;Predecessor&quot; refers to Mariner Energy Inc which was formerly called Hardy Oil &amp; Gas USA Inc prior to the effective date of its acquisition by Mariner Holdings Inc effective in April 1996.</p>
<p>The company said that price increases subsequent to March 1997 were sufficient to avoid the impairment charge, but the company elected to record the charge in the first quarter of 1997 in order to reduce the risk of future impairments and to conservatively state the book value of its assets. The impairment charge was determined under full cost accounting rules based on temporary decline in oil and gas prices during March 1997.</p>
